            <ArticleTitle>Septicaemia and endomyocarditis caused by Aerococcus urinae.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>446-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aerococcus urinae, an uncommon urinary tract pathogen, was recently shown to cause septicaemia and endocarditis in a few patients in Denmark and the Netherlands. In Austria this is the first report of a fatal course of endomyocarditis by Aerococcus urinae, associated with multiple septic infarcts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
